/P 48 0 R
/T (The project will follow four steps: understand the business, collect the data, clean and analyse it, and draw recommendations. Two to three meetings with the owner, with field notes of each, will confirm the problem, because the owner knows the seasons, the guests and the earlier efforts better than any outside source. Occupancy trend analysis by month and weekday, with a comparison of the festive, winter and other months, will show when rooms remain empty. Revenue analysis by room type will show how much the AC and non-AC rooms earn. A comparison of tariff, occupancy and revenue per available room will show whether the current rates suit each season. Grouping guests by arrival day and length of stay will show how walk-in guests behave. Each method matches one problem statement.)
/E (The project will follow four steps: understand the business, collect the data, clean and analyse it, and draw recommendations. Two to three meetings with the owner, with field notes of each, will confirm the problem, because the owner knows the seasons, the guests and the earlier efforts better than any outside source. Occupancy trend analysis by month and weekday, with a comparison of the festive, winter and other months, will show when rooms remain empty. Revenue analysis by room type will show how much the AC and non-AC rooms earn. A comparison of tariff, occupancy and revenue per available room will show whether the current rates suit each season. Grouping guests by arrival day and length of stay will show how walk-in guests behave. Each method matches one problem statement.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
