/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (Only primary data will be collected, directly from the guest house. The project will gather as many months of records as the notebooks hold, ideally 12 to 24 months, covering check-in and check- out dates, room number and type, tariff charged, number of guests, length of stay, discounts given and payment mode. Monthly operating expenses such as electricity, staff salaries, laundry and maintenance will come from the owner's bills. These variables match the problem statements: dates and room type for occupancy, arrival and stay details for walk-in guests, tariff and discounts for pricing, and the notebooks themselves for record quality. Handwritten entries will be typed into a spreadsheet with a metadata sheet that describes each column. Guest names, phone numbers and identity details will not be collected, which protects guest privacy. A signed letter from the owner, photographs of the property and a short video interaction with the owner will prove that the data is original.)
/E (Only primary data will be collected, directly from the guest house. The project will gather as many months of records as the notebooks hold, ideally 12 to 24 months, covering check-in and check- out dates, room number and type, tariff charged, number of guests, length of stay, discounts given and payment mode. Monthly operating expenses such as electricity, staff salaries, laundry and maintenance will come from the owner's bills. These variables match the problem statements: dates and room type for occupancy, arrival and stay details for walk-in guests, tariff and discounts for pricing, and the notebooks themselves for record quality. Handwritten entries will be typed into a spreadsheet with a metadata sheet that describes each column. Guest names, phone numbers and identity details will not be collected, which protects guest privacy. A signed letter from the owner, photographs of the property and a short video interaction with the owner will prove that the data is original.)
