381 0 obj
<<
/Title (Internal causes. Bookings are recorded informally in small handwritten notebooks, which makes it hard to total monthly revenue or compare one month with another. With only three staff members, of whom one is the receptionist, there may be little time to maintain detailed records. The guest house also takes no online bookings, so every guest has to walk in. External causes. Tourism in Jodhpur is seasonal, with the busiest periods in the festive and winter seasons and quieter months in between. Many hotels and guest houses near the bus stand and the railway station compete for the same travellers, and many travellers now compare options and book rooms online, which a walk-in-only guest house may miss.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 276 0 R
/Prev 326 0 R
/Next 327 0 R
>>
endobj
382 0 obj
<<
/Title (Only primary data will be collected, directly from the guest house. The project will gather as many months of records as the notebooks hold, ideally 12 to 24 months, covering check-in and check- out dates, room number and type, tariff charged, number of guests, length of stay, discounts given and payment mode. Monthly operating expenses such as electricity, staff salaries, laundry and maintenance will come from the owner's bills. These variables match the problem statements: dates and room type for occupancy, arrival and stay details for walk-in guests, tariff and discounts for pricing, and the notebooks themselves for record quality. Handwritten entries will be typed into a spreadsheet with a metadata sheet that describes each column. Guest names, phone numbers and identity details will not be collected, which protects guest privacy. A signed letter from the owner, photographs of the property and a short video interaction with the owner will prove that the data is original.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 329 0 R
>>
endobj
